<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nursultan Nazarbayev</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. <a href="/years/1940">1940</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nursultan Nazarbayev became first secretary of the Communist Party of the Kazakh SSR in 1989 and led Kazakhstan to independence in December 1991. As president until 2019 he dominated politics, built a new capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/astana">Astana</a> and steered an oil-based economy. He kept great influence after stepping down until the unrest of January 2022 reduced his power.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nursultan-nazarbayev.jpg" alt="Nursultan Nazarbayev" width="320" height="428" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Official website of the President of Russia · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%D0%92%D1%81%D1%82%D1%80%D0%B5%D1%87%D0%B0_%D1%81_%D0%9D%D1%83%D1%80%D1%81%D1%83%D0%BB%D1%82%D0%B0%D0%BD%D0%BE%D0%BC_%D0%9D%D0%B0%D0%B7%D0%B0%D1%80%D0%B1%D0%B0%D0%B5%D0%B2%D1%8B%D0%BC_(2025-05-29)_3_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
